\[
k\in\{0,1,\dots ,n-2\}\quad\text{or}\quad k\in\{2,3,\dots ,n-2\},
\] 
and then eliminate the impossible values by a parity/covering argument (using the condition that every lattice point \((a,b)\) with \(a+b\le n+1\) must lie on some line).

